review_comments.body:
This is pretty much a styling nit, but this might be better done with a base set that is extended if tk is too new:

```suggestion
    _no_round = {'padx', 'pady'}
    _clipped = {'highlightthickness'}
    if tk_version >= (9, 0):
        _no_round.update(
            {
                'borderwidth',
                'height',
                'highlightthickness',
                'width',
            }
        )
        _clipped.update(_no_round)
```

Or as a single

```
if tk_version < (9, 0):
    # set stuff
else:
    # set stuff
```

branch.  The two ternaries back-to-back aren't especially readable to me :)

